   "fieldtype": "HTML",
   "label": "Certificate Help",
   "options": "<div class=\"frappe-sign-settings-note\">\n    <h4>PDF signing certificate</h4>\n\n    <p>\n        Certificate-based PDF signing uses a dedicated document-signing certificate.\n        This is different from the SSL/TLS certificate used by your website domain.\n    </p>\n\n    <p>\n        <strong>Self-signed certificate:</strong>\n        suitable for internal integrity checks and audit evidence. External PDF viewers\n        may show the signature as unknown or untrusted unless the certificate is manually trusted.\n    </p>\n\n    <p>\n        <strong>CA-issued document-signing certificate:</strong>\n        suitable for external-facing documents when issued by a recognised document-signing\n        certificate authority or trust service provider. This is not the same as a normal\n        domain SSL certificate.\n    </p>\n\n    <p>\n        Let\u2019s Encrypt certificates are intended for HTTPS/TLS server authentication and should\n        not be used as PDF document-signing certificates.\n    </p>\n</div>"
